derived from attributed implementation responsibilities\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"M-runtime-contract\",\n    \"M-runtime-errors\",\n    \"M-actor\",\n    \"M-log-doc\"\n  ],\n  \"pending\": [],\n  \"assessment\": \"unassessed\",\n  \"candidate\": true,\n  \"grounding\": {\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"M-actor\",\n      \"M-storage-read\"\n    ],\n    \"expectation_ids\": [\n      \"M-runtime-contract\",\n      \"M-runtime-errors\",\n      \"M-log-doc\"\n    ],\n    \"binding_ids\": [],\n    \"derivation\": \"append_notify explicitly awaits its entry's decided index. Its Superseded documentation permits conservative error when the original entry may survive; it does not authorize successful completion for a different entry. Decided content is stable under the core log contract. Assignment index is the accepted exclusive boundary, so position k-1 is checked in an uncompacted log.\",\n    \"applicability\": \"One actually admitted operation and its own future; success is the implication antecedent, not an admission filter.\",\n    \"unresolved\": [],\n    \"conflicts\": [],\n    \"alternatives\": [\n      \"Superseded or another error is not a false success and therefore satisfies the bounded implication only.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"version\": 1\n}\nFIXED PLAN {\n  \"description\": \"Isolate the old leader's sole unchosen entry, form a new quorum on the other two nodes, decide a different value, then heal through documented reconnect callbacks and genuine Prepare/AcceptSync before the next origin actor notification tick. Observe the exact original future and decided entry content after completion.\",\n  \"claim_id\": \"C-notify-identity\",\n  \"binding_ids\": [\n    \"BND-notify\"\n  ],\n  \"monitors\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"MON-notify\",\n      \"checker_id\": \"CHK-notify\",\n      \"event\": \"result\",\n      \"binding_ids\": [\n        \"BND-notify\"\n      ],\n      \"grounding\": {\n        \"source_ids\": [\n          \"M-actor\",\n          \"M-runtime-io\",\n          \"M-storage-read\"\n        ],\n        \"expectation_ids\": [\n          \"M-runtime-contract\",\n          \"M-runtime-errors\"\n        ],\n        \"binding_ids\": [\n          \"BND-notify\"\n        ],\n        \"derivation\": \"admitted is emitted after authentic AcceptDecide messages demonstrate acceptance of the only notify call, while its future remains pending and local decided index is zero. The result joins that exact future and then reads actor-owned decided contents through the read command. Operation/scenario identity is independent of compared content and changing ballot. actual_value is read at returned_index-1; -1 denotes no such entry and differs from the positive input domain.\",\n        \"applicability\": \"Single unbatched, uncompacted operation with real message history and no concurrent application proposals after replacement.\",\n        \"unresolved\": [],\n        \"conflicts\": [],\n        \"alternatives\": [\n          \"An error is completed but does not assert that the submitted value was decided.\"\n        ]\n      },\n      \"applicability_conditions\": [],\n      \"admission_alias\": \"admission\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"observable_properties\": [\n    {\n      \"checker_id\": \"CHK-notify\",\n      \"kind\": \"event_implication\",\n      \"trigger\": {\n        \"field\": \"completed\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": true,\n        \"reference\": null\n      },\n      \"assertion\": {\n        \"field\": \"actual_value\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": null,\n        \"reference\": \"admission.requested_value\"\n      },\n      \"antecedent\": {\n        \"field\": \"ok\",\n        \"op\": \"eq\",\n        \"value\": true,\n        \"reference\": null\n      },\n      \"identity_fields\": [\n        \"scenario\",\n        \"operation\"\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"For the admitted call, observed successful completion implies that the decided entry at its returned assigned position equals the submitted value. Errors satisfy only this implication; missing results remain unknown.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"uncertainties\": [\n    \"No universal consensus-safety conclusion, crash guarantee or deadline proof.\",\n    \"The construction exploration saw a discrepancy but does not supply this fixed check's Evidence.\"\n  ]\n}\nharness identical True\n    32\t}\n    33\tfn initial_pump(nodes: &mut [Option<Op>]) {\n    34\t    let mut q=VecDeque::new();\n    35\t    for _ in 0..100 {\n    36\t        take_raw(nodes, &mut q);\n    37\t        if q.is_empty() {return;}\n    38\t        while let Some(m)=q.pop_front() {println!(\"TRACE route {:?}\",m);let to=m.get_receiver() as usize-1; nodes[to].as_mut().unwrap().handle_incoming(m);}\n    39\t    }\n    40\t    panic!(\"initial network failed to quiesce\");\n    41\t}\n    42\t#[tokio::test(flavor=\"current_thread\")]\n    43\tasync fn check_notification_identity_after_replacement() {\n    44\t    let mut nodes=vec![Some(node(1)),Some(node(2)),Some(node(3))];\n    45\t    nodes[0].as_mut().unwrap().try_become_leader();\n    46\t    initial_pump(&mut nodes);\n    47\t    assert_eq!(nodes[0].as_ref().unwrap().get_current_leader(),Some((1,true)));\n    48\t    assert!(nodes.iter().flatten().all(|n|n.get_decided_idx()==0 && n.get_accepted_idx()==0));\n    49\t    println!(\"CA_EVENT {{\\\"event\\\":\\\"initial\\\",\\\"leader\\\":1,\\\"accepted\\\":0,\\\"decided\\\":0}}\");\n    50\t    // A long but finite actor tick allows real protocol messages to be handled\n    51\t    // between notification evaluations. No actor internals or timer flags are changed.\n    52\t    let cfg=RuntimeConfig {tick_period:Duration::from_secs(10),egress_period:Duration::from_millis(1),append_notify_timeout:Duration::from_secs(25),..Default::default()};\n    53\t    let h=spawn_actor::<_,_,Runtime>(nodes[0].take().unwrap(),cfg);\n    54\t    let out=h.outgoing_messages();\n    55\t    let hc=h.clone();\n    56\t    let call=tokio::spawn(async move {hc.append_notify(Value(101)).await});\n    57\t    let mut dropped=0;\n    58\t    let requested_value=101u64;\n    59\t    tokio::time::timeout(Duration::from_secs(2), async {\n    60\t        while dropped < 2 {\n    61\t            let m=out.recv().await.unwrap();\n    62\t            println!(\"TRACE partition_drop {:?}\",m);\n    63\t            if let Message::SequencePaxos(p)=&m {\n    64\t                if let PaxosMsg::AcceptDecide(a)=&p.msg {\n    65\t                    assert_eq!(a.entries,vec![Value(101)]);\n    66\t                    dropped+=1;\n    67\t                    println!(\"CA_EVENT {{\\\"event\\\":\\\"isolated_accept\\\",\\\"from\\\":{},\\\"to\\\":{},\\\"value\\\":101,\\\"ballot_n\\\":{}}}\",p.from,p.to,a.n.n);\n    68\t                }\n    69\t            }\n    70\t            // Partition node 1: no outgoing packet is delivered to nodes 2/3.\n    71\t        }\n    72\t    }).await.expect(\"original proposal must produce actual acceptance messages\");\n    73\t    assert!(!call.is_finished());\n    74\t    assert_eq!(h.decided_idx().await,0);\n    75\t    println!(\"CA_EVENT {{\\\"event\\\":\\\"admitted\\\",\\\"scenario\\\":\\\"replacement\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"notify-A\\\",\\\"requested_value\\\":{},\\\"origin\\\":1,\\\"admitted\\\":true}}\", requested_value);\n    76\t    // Nodes 2 and 3 form a new quorum without the isolated node's unchosen A.\n    77\t    nodes[1].as_mut().unwrap().try_become_leader();\n    78\t    let mut q=VecDeque::new();\n    79\t    for _ in 0..50 {\n    80\t        take_raw(&mut nodes,&mut q);\n    81\t        if q.is_empty(){break;}\n    82\t        while let Some(m)=q.pop_front(){println!(\"TRACE route {:?}\",m);let to=m.get_receiver() as usize-1;if to!=0 {nodes[to].as_mut().unwrap().handle_incoming(m);}}\n    83\t    }\n    84\t    assert_eq!(nodes[1].as_ref().unwrap().get_current_leader(),Some((2,true)));\n    85\t    nodes[1].as_mut().unwrap().append(Value(202)).unwrap();\n    86\t    for _ in 0..50 {\n    87\t        take_raw(&mut nodes,&mut q);\n    88\t        if q.is_empty(){break;}\n    89\t        while let Some(m)=q.pop_front(){println!(\"TRACE route {:?}\",m);let to=m.get_receiver() as usize-1;if to!=0 {nodes[to].as_mut().unwrap().handle_incoming(m);}}\n    90\t    }\n    91\t    assert_eq!(nodes[1].as_ref().unwrap().get_decided_idx(),1);\n    92\t    assert_eq!(nodes[2].as_ref().unwrap().get_decided_idx(),1);\n    93\t    println!(\"CA_EVENT {{\\\"event\\\":\\\"replacement_decided\\\",\\\"leader\\\":2,\\\"value\\\":202,\\\"decided\\\":1}}\");\n    94\t    // Heal links with the documented reconnect callbacks. Drain and dispatch\n    95\t    // each sender's emitted stream in order; every delivered packet is genuine.\n    96\t    h.reconnected(2).await;\n    97\t    h.reconnected(3).await;\n    98\t    nodes[1].as_mut().unwrap().reconnected(1);\n    99\t    nodes[2].as_mut().unwrap().reconnected(1);\n   100\t    let mut sync_seen=false;\n   101\t    tokio::time::timeout(Duration::from_secs(2),async {\n   102\t        loop {\n   103\t            while let Ok(m)=out.try_recv(){println!(\"TRACE actor_emitted {:?}\",m);q.push_back(m);}\n   104\t            take_raw(&mut nodes,&mut q);\n   105\t            while let Some(m)=q.pop_front(){\n   106\t                println!(\"TRACE route {:?}\",m);let to=m.get_receiver() as usize-1;\n   107\t                if to==0 {\n   108\t                    if let Message::SequencePaxos(p)=&m {if let PaxosMsg::AcceptSync(a)=&p.msg {\n   109\t                        sync_seen=true;\n   110\t                        println!(\"CA_EVENT {{\\\"event\\\":\\\"sync_delivered\\\",\\\"ballot_n\\\":{},\\\"decided\\\":{},\\\"suffix\\\":{:?}}}\",a.n.n,a.decided_idx,a.log_sync.suffix.iter().map(|v|v.0).collect::<Vec<_>>());\n   111\t                    }}\n   112\t                    h.handle_incoming(m).await;\n   113\t                } else {nodes[to].as_mut().unwrap().handle_incoming(m);}\n   114\t            }\n   115\t            if h.decided_idx().await==1 {break;}\n   116\t            tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_millis(1)).await;\n   117\t        }\n   118\t    }).await.expect(\"origin must install replacement before notifier tick\");\n   119\t    assert!(sync_seen);\n   120\t    let read=h.read_decided_suffix(0).await.unwrap();\n   121\t    let values:Vec<u64>=read.iter().filter_map(|e|match e{LogEntry::Decided(v)=>Some(v.0),_=>None}).collect();\n   122\t    assert_eq!(values,vec![202]);\n   123\t    println!(\"CA_EVENT {{\\\"event\\\":\\\"origin_read\\\",\\\"values\\\":{:?},\\\"call_finished_before_tick\\\":{}}}\",values,call.is_finished());\n   124\t    // Keep the healed transport and raw-node clocks serviced until the actor\n   125\t    // returns. Completion is read before shutdown; a wait failure is not a result.\n   126\t    let raw_clock=tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_secs(10));\n   127\t    tokio::pin!(raw_clock);\n   128\t    tokio::time::timeout(Duration::from_secs(15),async {\n   129\t        loop {\n   130\t            while let Ok(m)=out.try_recv(){println!(\"TRACE actor_emitted {:?}\",m);q.push_back(m);}\n   131\t            take_raw(&mut nodes,&mut q);\n   132\t            while let Some(m)=q.pop_front(){\n   133\t                println!(\"TRACE route {:?}\",m);\n   134\t                let to=m.get_receiver() as usize-1;\n   135\t                if to==0 {h.handle_incoming(m).await;} else {nodes[to].as_mut().unwrap().handle_incoming(m);}\n   136\t            }\n   137\t            if call.is_finished(){break;}\n   138\t            tokio::select! {\n   139\t                _=&mut raw_clock=>{\n   140\t                    for n in nodes.iter_mut().flatten(){n.tick();}\n   141\t                    raw_clock.as_mut().reset(tokio::time::Instant::now()+Duration::from_secs(10));\n   142\t                }\n   143\t                _=tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_millis(1))=>{}\n   144\t            }\n   145\t        }\n   146\t    }).await.expect(\"notification must return a result within observation bound\");\n   147\t    let result=call.await.unwrap();\n   148\t    let (ok,returned_index,error)=match result {\n   149\t        Ok(idx)=>(true,idx,\"none\"),\n   150\t        Err(omnipaxos_runtime::AppendError::Superseded{..})=>(false,0,\"superseded\"),\n   151\t        Err(omnipaxos_runtime::AppendError::Timeout)=>(false,0,\"timeout\"),\n   152\t        Err(omnipaxos_runtime::AppendError::Shutdown)=>(false,0,\"shutdown\"),\n   153\t        Err(_)=>(false,0,\"other\"),\n   154\t    };\n   155\t    // All state reads are actor commands. No caller writes log values, injects\n   156\t    // ballots/messages, or samples mutable protocol fields concurrently.\n   157\t    let final_decided=h.decided_idx().await;\n   158\t    let final_read=h.read_decided_suffix(0).await.unwrap();\n   159\t    let final_values:Vec<u64>=final_read.iter().filter_map(|e|match e{LogEntry::Decided(v)=>Some(v.0),_=>None}).collect();\n   160\t    // accepted_idx/decided_idx and runtime assignments are exclusive boundaries:\n   161\t    // the assigned first entry has return value 1 and core read position 0.\n   162\t    let actual_value=returned_index.checked_sub(1).and_then(|i|final_values.get(i)).map(|v|*v as i64).unwrap_or(-1);\n   163\t    println!(\"CA_EVENT {{\\\"event\\\":\\\"result\\\",\\\"scenario\\\":\\\"replacement\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"notify-A\\\",\\\"completed\\\":true,\\\"ok\\\":{},\\\"returned_index\\\":{},\\\"error\\\":\\\"{}\\\",\\\"actual_value\\\":{},\\\"decided_idx\\\":{},\\\"decided_values\\\":{:?}}}\",ok,returned_index,error,actual_value,final_decided,final_values);\n   164\t    drop(h);\n   165\t    drop(out);\n   166\t    let join=ACTOR.lock().unwrap().take().unwrap();\n   167\t    tokio::time::timeout(Duration::from_secs(2),join).await.expect(\"actor shutdown\").expect(\"actor did not panic\");\n   168\t    println!(\"CA_EVENT {{\\\"event\\\":\\\"cleanup\\\",\\\"actor_joined\\\":true}}\");\n   169\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The fixed check recorded the same identity mismatch, then failed while waiting for actor shutdown after all completion observations were recorded. I’ll review the completed witness separately and retain the two-second shutdown timeout as an unresolved lifecycle observation. It does not by itself establish permanent nontermination.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=dict(action='review',artifact_id='7b63c5fa750747b29543e17e6b7da0d2',rationale='Review the fixed current artifact and complete identity counterexample, explicitly separating its post-observation cleanup failure.',review_items=[dict(aspect='checker_correspondence',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=['M-runtime-contract','M-runtime-errors','M-actor','M-runtime-io','M-runtime-trait','M-public','M-leader','M-follower','M-sync-storage','M-storage-read','M-memory-storage'],rationale='Reviewed Claim C-notify-identity v1, fixed plan and exact harness bytes for artifact 7b63c5fa750747b29543e17e6b7da0d2, and raw CheckRun d6c6f213390745ee9884b2c7b71b96c1. Applicability: append_notify promises its entry\\\\'s decided index; Superseded is expressly a conservative error, not permission for an unrelated successful result. The runtime assigns accepted_after, an exclusive boundary; first entry maps returned 1 to core position 0. Entry content, not just index/count, is compared. History: empty three-node cores first complete genuine ballot-1 Prepare/Promise/AcceptSync. The exact node-1 instance is moved into the actor. The only notification call proposes 101; both emitted AcceptDecide packets containing 101 are dropped by the node-1 partition, while nodes 2/3 remain empty. Public try_become_leader on node 2 generates ballot 2; the trace records node-3 promise and acceptance, then 202 at boundary 1 is decided by nodes 2/3. Caller reconnect callbacks generate PrepareReq, Prepare, Promise and AcceptSync; received synchronization carries decided=1, sync_idx=0 and suffix [202]. No target state or message is fabricated. Draining sender buffers preserves remaining per-link ordering; the partition routing label TRACE route is an attempted route and the fixed conditional explicitly drops destination 1 during isolation. Origin actor commands verify actual installation [202], so mere enqueue/sync_seen is not used alone as completion. Identity: one task owns one future; admission and result both use independent scenario=replacement, operation=notify-A, not the compared value or changed ballot. The monitor selects admission explicitly. Admission is emitted after real acceptance and before replacement; the result is emitted only after joining the original future. Observed ok=true, returned_index=1, actual_value=202 and admission requested_value=101 make the implication false. Reads occur through actor-owned commands while the actor is live and no later application proposals exist. The post-result decided suffix confirms content independently of expectation. No missing result, parse error, or correlation ambiguity is present. Cause evidence: drain_notifiers success branch ignores stored ballot and precedes Superseded; incoming dispatch processes Prepare/AcceptSync without notification until a tick. Thus the measured history exercises the original discriminator rather than an easier substitute. Failure analysis: stderr points solely to fixed harness line 167, actor shutdown Elapsed, after the result event at line 163 and handle drops at 164-165. It is not a target panic, unfulfilled admission, missing operation completion or unreliable shutdown-state read. The cleanup event was not emitted and normal actor shutdown is NOT established. This independently bounded lifecycle observation does not reverse an already-returned success or decided value, so the complete identity witness survives the nonzero process exit.',counterevidence=['The existing Superseded branch would conservatively fail a call if a notifier tick observed new promise before the assigned position became decided; this schedule legally dispatches both transition and synchronization before that tick.','Quorum adoption protects potentially chosen entries. Here 101 only reached isolated node 1; the majority 2/3 legitimately chose 202, so the mismatch is a runtime success-attribution defect rather than demonstrated core agreement failure.','The run ended with exit 101 because post-result actor join exceeded the harness\\\\'s two-second cleanup window. This failure and absent cleanup event are retained; no universal shutdown conclusion is inferred.'],limitations=['One unbatched, uncompacted, local-origin append_notify in a fixed three-node configuration with MemoryStorage, no restart.','Finite explicit leadership transition via public API and real timer interval; no deadline violation or global progress proof.','Does not establish all runtime notification variants or overall core consensus unsafety.','Actor shutdown did not complete in the two-second post-observation wait; cleanup ownership and closed-stream selection need separate investigation.'],report_title='日志替换后原写入仍返回成功',report_answer='固定执行中，值 101 的 append_notify 返回 Ok(1)，但该位置已由新任期决定为 202。消息来自真实三节点协议执行，原写入未到达多数派；现有 Superseded 分支未阻止此次错误成功。观测完成后的 actor 退出等待另行超时，未据此推断永久无法退出。')],feedback=dict(ref_ids=['d6c6f213390745ee9884b2c7b71b96c1','739a7fe5e829431788df0e6cbe41428f','7b63c5fa750747b29543e17e6b7da0d2','F-assignment','B-runtime-notification','M-actor'],answered='The fixed execution produced a fully correlated false success: admission requested 101; the joined original notification returned Ok(1); the live origin actor then reported decided index 1 and decided content [202]. The monitor comparison was violated with complete witness and no parsing errors. Exit 101 came afterward from the harness\\\\'s actor-join timeout, not from the comparison or its prerequisites.',remaining=['Controller assessment after correspondence review.','Independently investigate why actor join did not complete after handles were dropped; the finite timeout alone does not establish a shutdown violation.'],understanding='updated',rationale='No predicate, requirement or setup change is needed to assess the complete identity witness. Keep the post-observation lifecycle failure explicit instead of deleting it or pretending process success.',question_updates={'739a7fe5e829431788df0e6cbe41428f':dict(unknowns=['Correspondence now reviewed for the fixed local-origin identity witness; controller assessment remains authoritative. Independent shutdown timeout is outside this identity proposition.'],resume_conditions=[])}))\njson.dump(s,open('submission-review-notify.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-06_19-56-06-omnipaxos-real-run --submission submission-review-notify.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
